cff-version: 1.2.0
type: dataset
title: "Comparative RNA-seq Analysis of Vaccinated and Unvaccinated Individuals Infected with SARS-CoV-2"
authors:
  - family-names: Chinhema
    given-names: Simbisai
    affiliation: "Bioinformatics"
date-released: 2026-07-26
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
url: https://github.com/simbisaichinhema/RNA-seq-Differential-Expression-Analysis-DESeq2
repository-url: https://github.com/simbisaichinhema/RNA-seq-Differential-Expression-Analysis-DESeq2
contributors:
  - family-names: Chinhema
    given-names: Simbisai
    affiliation: "Bioinformatics"
keywords:
  - RNA-seq
  - SARS-CoV-2
  - DESeq2
  - differential expression
  - functional enrichment
  - GSE201530
  - transcriptomics
  - COVID-19
  - vaccinated
  - unvaccinated
abstract: |
  A reproducible bioinformatics workflow for comparative RNA-seq analysis of
  vaccinated and unvaccinated individuals infected with SARS-CoV-2, using
  DESeq2 for differential expression and clusterProfiler for functional
  enrichment. Data sourced from GEO dataset GSE201530.
references:
  - doi: 10.1093/nar/gkab1059
    title: "RNA-seq analysis of SARS-CoV-2 vaccinated and unvaccinated individuals"
  - doi: 10.1093/nar/gkac1005
    title: "DESeq2: a Bioconductor package for differential expression analysis of genomic data using R"
  - doi: 10.1093/nar/gkab1087
    title: "clusterProfiler: an R package for comparing biological themes among gene clusters"
  - doi: 10.1093/bioinformatics/bty663
    title: "pathview: an R/Bioconductor package for pathway-based data integration and visualization"
